This subdirectory 'fit' contains input and output of fits with finite-range
pairing. 

It contains sample input in the file 'for001.<name>' and corresponding
output in the file 'for002.<name>' where '<name>' is an obvious name
describing the actual case. The name is derived from the corresponding
functional with soft cutoff pairing. The ending 'all' means a refit of
all model parameters, while 'pairpar' indicates a fit where only the
pairing parameters had been re-fitted.

The fits are preformed by the routine 'hffit.exe' which was compiled
in the main directory with './clfit'. The fitting routine handles input
and output with fixed file names:
 'for010'    = input for basic pool of fit data,
 'for009'    = input for choice of difference data,
 'for001'    = input for detailed instructions (selection of data from 
               data files, model options, starting parameters, ...),
 'for002'    = output of fit protocol (steps, covariance matrices, 
               table with final results).
If one want to (re-)do a fit from the given 'for001.<name>', one must
copy 'for001.<name>' to for001,  'for009.<name>' to for009, and
'for010.<name>' to for010. Then one can issue a 
'<base-directory>/hffit.exe > /dev/null'. (Without the '/dev/null', the
code will print a lot of grab to the screen.)´

The 'hffit.exe' is a sequential code and can be slow, particularly in
connection with HFB calculations. The exists an OpenMP version. It can
be generated with './clfit_omp' which produces an executable 'hffit.omp'.
To run this, one must have a copy of the HF routine 'haforpa.exe' in
the woring directory. This exectuable is produced by 'clrpa' in the
base directory. It then can either be copied to the working directory
or linked.


So far, the following cases are deposited:

SVmin-softcut         original SV-min with soft cutoff of
                      window approximately 5 MeV.

SVmin-width15         refit SV-min with finite-range pairing
                      of width 1.5 fm, window 100 MeV

FyIVPeven-softcut     originval Fy(IVP) with soft cutoff
                      window 15 MeV
FyIVPeven-width15     refit Fy(IVP) with finite-range pairing
                      of width 1.5 fm, window 100 MeV
                      


